        "content": "## Required setup\n\n1. Put the master CV at `/home/node/.n8n-files/document-pipeline/master_cv.json`.\n2. Ensure `/opt/n8n/document-pipeline` is available inside the n8n container at the same path.\n3. Install the verified community node `@apify/n8n-nodes-apify`.\n4. Select the Apify actor **LinkedIn Jobs Scraper | Remove Duplicate Jobs | Pay Per Result** in the Apify node.\n5. Attach your existing Baserow, Apify, OpenRouter, Cloudinary, and Baserow Header Auth credentials.\n6. This workflow assumes table IDs:\n   - Jobs: `1098021`\n   - Search Criteria: `1098022`\n   - Prompts: `1098023`\n7. The Jobs REST write uses field names. Add these Baserow columns if they do not exist:\n   - `CV TEX URL`\n   - `Cover Letter TEX URL`\n\nThe four generated files share one application ID:\n- `cv_<application-id>.pdf`\n- `cv_<application-id>.tex`\n- `cover-letter_<application-id>.pdf`\n- `cover-letter_<application-id>.tex`\n\n\n## Baserow file uploads\n\nThe workflow first uploads each Cloudinary secure URL to Baserow through\n`/api/user-files/upload-via-url/`, then inserts the returned Baserow file names\ninto the native Baserow Create Row node.\n\nEach file column receives two attachments:\n- CV: PDF and TEX\n- Cover Letter: PDF and TEX\n\nThe `Baserow API Token` HTTP Header Auth credential must send:\n- Header name: `Authorization`\n- Header value: `Token YOUR_BASEROW_DATABASE_TOKEN`\n\n\n## Fail-soft processing\n\nAfter the initial Baserow row is created, failures in content generation, document rendering, any of the four Baserow file uploads, upload merging, file-update payload construction, or the final Baserow update are routed back to **Loop Over Jobs**. The metadata-only row remains stored and processing continues with the next job.\n",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 1700
      },
